 life and just figure  out what i was actually understanding  about myself he likes to call himself an  explorer not a teacher his latest new  york times bestselling book lays out how  to find clarity and connection something  he struggled with for much of his life i  never wanted to admit to myself that i  actually felt pretty sad and depressed  inside what was the rock bottom moment  for you  just partying way too much doing too  many different drugs and just pushing  myself  way too far i felt like my life was like  slipping  from reality so i took the drugs i  flushed them down the toilet and from  that day forward that's when all the  honesty started he says vipassana  meditation which means to see things as  they really are  changed his life it's now the biggest  part of his identity and backbone of his  work meditation made me realize that i  don't need to cause myself this extra  mental pain the moment you allow what  happened to strengthen you  you win  vulnerability and pain are also at the  center of delia's work i was  at the threshold of taking my own life i  was in depression coming from back to  back domestic violence partnerships it  was a lot and i didn't know how to  express that pain and i didn't know how  to stop down spiraling and so breaking  that cycle for me was the turning point  so many of us come to our higher selves  through pain through that portal dalia  has amassed more than a half million  followers doing what she loves as a  spiritual writer  what's it like for you to be back at the  beach a place you like to write  feels like home  she encourages people to vibrate higher  daily aptly the title of her new book  it just means that day after day that  you have this  commitment and your actions are an  affirmation they're a meditation they're  offerings to this commitment to  live at a higher level just remember who  you are and remember your practice it  seems like for a lot of people part of  the practice now is going to instagram  to writers spaces like yours and looking  at it and feeling inspired for the day  absolutely like getting messages from  people saying that i was going to give  up  you know your words help me this right  here it lets me know that i'm doing my  part to help the world vibrate higher in  some way there are now hundreds if not  thousands of accounts on instagram that  boast positive messages and while many  of these writers have secured book deals  through their success  the underlying goal and hope is simply  to help other people find their  happiness from within you talk a lot  about happiness doesn't come from a  relationship  a job  your family it comes from yourself yeah  can you help people understand that idea  a lot of happiness you know it has to be  cultivated from within you loving  yourself you being aligned with your  values and you also having a deep  appreciation of impermanence i think a  lot of the times the mental struggles  that we have are because we just reject  the fact that things are constantly  changing life is this  constant movement of change that we  don't really have control over do you  think that's why your writings are  speaking to so many people right now  absolutely i mean the world is a massive  transition everything's changing there  have always been problems historically  that people had to deal with but now we  have  a greater amount of accessibility in  regards to  accessing tools that can deeply heal  ourselves and that's what's always been  missing for cbs mornings jamie yukis in  los angeles  didn't you guys like the line misery is  going out of style yeah i like that a  lot and delia vibrate higher daily just  watching delia and jamie on the beach  together like that was pretty calming  yeah yeah and they're right change is  happening so quickly i think that's why  people are flocking to those messages of  support yeah vibrating highly higher be  around people that give you the great  vibrations exactly people that don't get  rid of them yeah all toxis all toxicity  out i so agree with that  all right good good good vibrations  speech voice that could be a song  and you can hear more of jamie's  conversation with diego and layla on the  cbs morning's podcast for now we'll be  right back  [Music]

